<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="UTF-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><meta name="theme-color" content="#142d4c"><meta name="description" content="Explore assistance programs available in Texas."><title>Texas Assistance Programs — American Aid Network</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/site.css"></head><body><?php require __DIR__ . "/../../includes/site-header.php"; ?><main><section class="state-page"><div class="wrap"><div class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/">Home</a><span>›</span><a href="/help/">Browse Programs</a><span>›</span><b>Texas</b></div><div class="state-intro"><div><h1>Assistance Programs in Texas</h1><p>11 programs, grouped by what you need help with. Each includes clear application guidance.</p></div><div><a class="button primary" href="/find/">Find my programs <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><small>Free · Private · Takes under 2 minutes</small></div></div><section class="program-group"><h2>Rent &amp; Housing Assistance</h2><div class="directory-cards"><article><h3>2-1-1 Texas</h3><p>Texas&#39;s statewide helpline for finding local assistance of every kind: rent, utility bills, food, shelter, and healthcare. Run by Texas Health and Human Services; dial 2-1-1 or call the toll-free line, with help in English and Spanish.</p><div><a href="/programs/2-1-1-texas/">How to apply <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href="/programs/2-1-1-texas/">Program details <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></article><article><h3>TexasLawHelp.org (Eviction &amp; Legal Help)</h3><p>Free legal information, forms, and guides for Texans, run by the nonprofit Texas Legal Services Center. The eviction section explains the notices, deadlines, and court steps, and connects you with legal aid.</p><div><a href="/programs/texaslawhelp-org-eviction-and-legal-help/">How to apply <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href="/programs/texaslawhelp-org-eviction-and-legal-help/">Program details <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></article></div><a class="group-cta" href="/find/">Check what you qualify for <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></section><section class="program-group"><h2>Utility Bill Help</h2><div class="directory-cards"><article><h3>CEAP (Comprehensive Energy Assistance Program)</h3><p>Texas&#39;s LIHEAP utility assistance: helps low-income households pay electric, gas, and propane bills, including in a shutoff crisis. Local agencies in all 254 counties take applications; find yours through TDHCA&#39;s Help for Texans page.</p><div><a href="/programs/ceap-comprehensive-energy-assistance-program/">How to apply <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href="/programs/ceap-comprehensive-energy-assistance-program/">Program details <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></article><article><h3>Weatherization Assistance Program (TDHCA)</h3><p>Free home energy improvements for low-income Texans: insulation, caulking, duct work, and repair or replacement of inefficient heating and cooling systems, so future bills shrink. Apply through the weatherization agency that serves your county.</p><div><a href="/programs/weatherization-assistance-program-tdhca/">How to apply <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href="/programs/weatherization-assistance-program-tdhca/">Program details <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></article></div><a class="group-cta" href="/find/">Check what you qualify for <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></section><section class="program-group"><h2>Cash Assistance &amp; Benefits</h2><div class="directory-cards"><article><h3>Child Care Services (TWC Scholarships)</h3><p>Child care scholarships that pay most of the cost of care for low-income working Texas families, run by the Texas Workforce Commission through local Workforce Solutions offices. Apply through childcare.texas.gov.</p><div><a href="/programs/child-care-services-twc-scholarships/">How to apply <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href="/programs/child-care-services-twc-scholarships/">Program details <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></article><article><h3>TWC Unemployment Benefits</h3><p>Temporary, partial income replacement if you lost your job or had hours cut through no fault of your own. Apply online through Unemployment Benefit Services or by phone at the TWC Tele-Center.</p><div><a href="/programs/twc-unemployment-benefits/">How to apply <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href="/programs/twc-unemployment-benefits/">Program details <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></article></div><a class="group-cta" href="/find/">Check what you qualify for <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></section><section class="program-group"><h2>Free &amp; Low-Cost Healthcare</h2><div class="directory-cards"><article><h3>Healthy Texas Women</h3><p>Free women&#39;s health services for uninsured Texas women 15 to 44: annual exams, family planning, and screenings and treatment for conditions like diabetes and high blood pressure. Use the site&#39;s Find a Doctor tool to locate a provider.</p><div><a href="/programs/healthy-texas-women/">How to apply <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href="/programs/healthy-texas-women/">Program details <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></article><article><h3>Texas Medicaid &amp; CHIP</h3><p>Free or low-cost health coverage for low-income Texas children, pregnant women, seniors, and people with disabilities. CHIP covers children in families that earn too much for Medicaid; one application at YourTexasBenefits.com checks both.</p><div><a href="/programs/texas-medicaid-and-chip/">How to apply <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href="/programs/texas-medicaid-and-chip/">Program details <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></article></div><a class="group-cta" href="/find/">Check what you qualify for <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></section><section class="program-group"><h2>Food Assistance</h2><div class="directory-cards"><article><h3>SNAP Food Benefits (Lone Star Card)</h3><p>Texas SNAP puts monthly grocery money on a Lone Star Card that works like a debit card at any store that accepts SNAP. Apply online at YourTexasBenefits.com or call 2-1-1 for help.</p><div><a href="/programs/snap-food-benefits-lone-star-card/">How to apply <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href="/programs/snap-food-benefits-lone-star-card/">Program details <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></article><article><h3>Texas WIC</h3><p>Healthy foods, breastfeeding support, and nutrition help for pregnant women, new mothers, and children under 5 in Texas. Apply online or find a local WIC office; benefits start at pregnancy and continue until a child turns 5.</p><div><a href="/programs/texas-wic/">How to apply <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href="/programs/texas-wic/">Program details <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></article></div><a class="group-cta" href="/find/">Check what you qualify for <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></section><section class="program-group"><h2>Crisis Support</h2><div class="directory-cards"><article><h3>TANF Cash Help</h3><p>Monthly cash payments for very-low-income Texas families with children 18 and younger, paid on the Lone Star Card. One-Time TANF also gives a single crisis payment, and certain relatives raising a child can get a once-in-a-lifetime $1,000 payment.</p><div><a href="/programs/tanf-cash-help/">How to apply <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href="/programs/tanf-cash-help/">Program details <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></article></div></section></div></section></main><footer><div class="wrap footer-grid"><div><a class="brand" href="/" aria-label="American Aid Network home"><span class="brand-mark" aria-hidden="true"><span>★</span><i></i><i></i><i></i></span><span>AMERICAN <b>AID</b><small>NETWORK</small></span></a><p>Clear, reliable guidance to assistance programs across America.</p><div class="verified">✓ Information from trusted sources</div></div><div><h4>FIND SUPPORT</h4><a href="/find/">Find help near me</a><a href="/help/">Browse by state</a><a href="/programs/">Program guides</a><a href="/#how-it-works">How it works</a></div><div><h4>ABOUT</h4><a href="/about/">Our mission</a><a href="/legal/contact/">Contact us</a><a href="/legal/privacy/">Privacy policy</a><a href="/legal/terms/">Terms of use</a></div></div><div class="wrap disclaimer">American Aid Network is an independent informational resource. We are not a government agency and do not administer benefit programs. Program details change; always confirm requirements with the official provider.<span>© 2026 American Aid Network</span></div></footer><script src="/assets/site.js" defer></script></body></html>